1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,389
Rain on a Saturday empties the shop.

2
00:00:03,189 --> 00:00:05,601
A home game packs the
street, or it doesn't.

3
00:00:06,151 --> 00:00:09,387
Either way, your week swings,
and you can't plan around it.

4
00:00:09,937 --> 00:00:13,424
Offset measures that swing in real
dollars, from your own revenue.

5
00:00:13,974 --> 00:00:17,030
Then it finds a Kalshi contract
that pays when it hits.

6
00:00:17,030 --> 00:00:17,863
And you decide.

7
00:00:18,413 --> 00:00:21,576
Here's a bike shop:
fictional sales, real weather.

8
00:00:21,576 --> 00:00:23,158
Upload its daily revenue.

9
00:00:23,808 --> 00:00:29,946
Rain costs it about $1,956 a day, and
that held up on data the model never saw.

10
00:00:31,146 --> 00:00:32,470
Knicks games? Nothing there.

11
00:00:32,470 --> 00:00:37,434
And a planted test effect lands inside the
model's interval, so the check is honest.

12
00:00:38,534 --> 00:00:41,414
The desk matches Kalshi's
Central Park rain contract,

13
00:00:41,414 --> 00:00:43,214
the same station we measured.

14
00:00:43,814 --> 00:00:47,907
It sizes protection to the
measured loss and never more:

15
00:00:47,907 --> 00:00:51,590
1,955 contracts, with the
full premium shown up front.

16
00:00:53,990 --> 00:00:56,131
But not every risk gets a hedge.

17
00:00:56,131 --> 00:00:59,800
For a taxi fleet, rain looked big
last year, then almost vanished.

18
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:02,552
So the desk says no, and shows you why.

19
00:01:04,852 --> 00:01:07,125
And nothing happens
until the owner approves.

20
00:01:08,525 --> 00:01:11,936
Every proposal, decline and
approval gets a receipt in the log.

21
00:01:12,486 --> 00:01:15,115
Approved hedges are booked
to a real ledger, and

22
00:01:15,115 --> 00:01:19,496
reconciliation catches a deposit that came
in short, and names the fee as the cause.

23
00:01:20,596 --> 00:01:22,854
The desk never approves its own hedge.

24
00:01:22,854 --> 00:01:25,758
Every number comes from
a tool, not the AI.

25
00:01:25,758 --> 00:01:28,016
And anything estimated
or simulated says so.

26
00:01:28,766 --> 00:01:31,324
Offset. Steadier weeks. Your call.

